 The builder is `view.Build(snapshot model.BoardSnapshot, asOf time.Time)`: it never reads the DB or the clock, so the live
 view (`cache.LoadCurrent`, now) and a future historical view (`history.LoadAsOf`, past instant) share it unchanged (ADR 0011).
 
+Addendum (ADR 0015): the ticket modal follows the same rule — `view.BuildTicket` returns a `TicketDetail` with ADF already
+parsed into a typed node tree (`internal/adf`), field values typed and grouped, and empty fields folded. TypeScript never
+parses raw ADF; its only content-derived computation is the per-theme `textColor` contrast clamp.
